-- title:
--   Unique formal completion of a Λ-linear morphism of fake elliptic curves
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, rationals $a,b$, a $\mathbb Z$-submodule $\Lambda$ of the quaternion algebra $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$, and a map $\mathrm{coord}\colon\Lambda\to\mathbb Z_{q^2}\times\mathbb Z_{q^2}$, where $\mathbb Z_{q^2}$ is the ring of Witt vectors of $\mathbb F_{q^2}$; assume $\mathrm{coord}$ has $q$-adically dense image, i.e. for every $k$ and every pair $(\alpha,\beta)$ there is $m\in\Lambda$ with both components of $\mathrm{coord}\,m$ congruent to $\alpha$, $\beta$ modulo the ideal generated by $q^k$. Let $N$ be a natural number and $B$ a commutative ring in which $q$ is nilpotent. Let $E,E'$ be fake elliptic curves of level $N$ over $B$ with $\Lambda$-action (schemes over $\operatorname{Spec} B$ with a commutative relative group law, an abelian-scheme property bundle, two-dimensional fibres, and an action of $\Lambda$), let $X,X'$ be formal $\mathcal O_D$-modules over $B$ (two-dimensional commutative formal group laws with an action of $\mathbb Z_{q^2}$ by one-variable substitution data and an endomorphism $\varpi$ with $\varpi\circ\varpi=[q]$ and $\varpi\circ[\alpha]=[\alpha^{\sigma}]\circ\varpi$), and let $\theta,\theta'$ be rank-$2$ formal coordinates for the structure morphisms of $E,E'$ such that `IsFormalModuleVia` holds: $\theta$ is a system of formal coordinates for the group law of $E$ with formal group $X.F$, and for all $m\in\Lambda$ and all points with coordinates in a nilpotent ideal, $\theta$ transports the action of $m$ on $E$ to the series $[\alpha_m]_X+[\beta_m]_X\circ\varpi_X$, where $(\alpha_m,\beta_m)=\mathrm{coord}\,m$; likewise for $\theta'$, $X'$, $E'$. Let $h$ be a morphism $E.A\to E'.A$ over $\operatorname{Spec} B$ which is additive on $T$-points for every $T\to\operatorname{Spec} B$ and satisfies $E.\mathrm{act}\,m$ followed by $h$ equals $h$ followed by $E'.\mathrm{act}\,m$ for all $m\in\Lambda$. Then there is a unique homomorphism $u\colon X\to X'$ of formal $\mathcal O_D$-modules whose underlying series is the formal completion of $h$ along $\theta,\theta'$, i.e. for every $B$-algebra $B'$, every ideal $J$ with $J^{n+1}=0$ and every $s\colon\mathrm{Fin}\,2\to J$, one has $\theta'\bigl(\text{truncated evaluation of }u\text{ at }s\bigr)=h\circ\theta(s)$ as points of $E'$ over the base.
--
--   This is the functoriality of the formal $\mathcal O_D$-module attached to a fake elliptic curve in the Čerednik–Drinfeld setting: a $\Lambda$-equivariant homomorphism of curves completes to a unique $\mathcal O_D$-linear homomorphism of the associated special formal modules. It is the input for the rigidification statements comparing fake elliptic curves with special formal modules, including the uniqueness of the formal module up to unique isomorphism and the analysis of $\Lambda$-linear endomorphisms.
